==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 60% HP:
**1 [[Master A.]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Since this stage plays out identically to [[Tapas Desert]], you can use the same strategy of luring Master A. to the [[Cat Base]], then taking out the peons so you can beat on him with tanky units such as [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]].

Stacking [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance units]] like [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]] and [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Medalist Cat]] at the beginning is another easy way to beat this stage, as all of the peons at the start are weak and low-range. [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]] also work, but be sure to only choose one or the other, as [[Wave Attack|Wave Attacks]] will surely clear the peons and cause your Long Distance units to walk into Master A.'s range.

